To configure your Nokia router's BGP to accept link-bandwidth extended community for IPv4 routes received from EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. This configuration enables the router to accept and use the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv4 routes received from all EBGP peers in the specified group.
