To configure a Nokia router to enable receiving BGP Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) capabilities from a peer during extended community negotiation, use the following CLI commands:

1. Enable outbound route filtering:
   ```
   configure router bgp outbound-route-filtering
   ```

2. Configure extended community support under outbound route filtering:
   ```
   extended-community
   ```

3. Enable the router to accept ORF filters from the peer:
   ```
   accept-orf
   ```

These commands will allow the router to negotiate and receive BGP ORF capabilities from the peer using extended communities.
