To configure Nokia routers to automatically add a link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
exit all
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This will enable the automatic addition of link-bandwidth extended communities to unlabeled IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers in the specified group.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
