To configure your Nokia router to automatically add a link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    link-bandwidth
        add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. This will enable the automatic addition of link-bandwidth extended communities to IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers in the specified group.
