To configure your Nokia router to allow BGP to propagate routes that are not currently selected as the best path in the routing table, use the following CLI commands:

1. Enable IBGP multipath to allow multiple paths for load balancing:
```
configure router bgp
    ibgp-multipath
exit
```

2. Configure best path selection to ignore router ID comparisons for certain path selections:
```
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    ignore-router-id include-internal mvpn-ipv4 mvpn-ipv6
exit
```

3. Enable outbound route filtering at the BGP group or neighbor level to ensure all routes are advertised regardless of best path status:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    outbound-route-filtering
exit
```

These configurations will allow BGP to propagate alternative paths even if they're not the current best path in the routing table.
------------
