To configure a Nokia router to allow BGP to propagate routes that are not the best path in the routing table, use the following CLI commands:

1. Enable IBGP multipath to allow multiple paths for load balancing:
```
configure router bgp
    ibgp-multipath
exit
```

2. Configure best-path-selection to ignore router ID comparisons for certain path selections:
```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-router-id
    exit
exit
```

These configurations will allow BGP to consider and propagate alternative paths beyond just the single best path in the routing table.
