Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to advertise VPN IPv4 and label IPv6 routes with an IPv6 address as the BGP next hop over an IPv6 transport session, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
# Configure BGP group or neighbor settings
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        family vpn-ipv4 label-ipv6
        extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4
        advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4 label-ipv6
        next-hop-self
        neighbor <neighbor-ipv6-address>
            enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
exit

# Configure next-hop resolution for labeled routes
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes
    allow-static
    transport-tunnel
        family label-ipv6
        family vpn
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ipv6-address>` with the IPv6 address of your BGP neighbor. This configuration enables the required capabilities and ensures proper next-hop handling for the specified route types over IPv6 transport.
