## User question:
How to configure Nokia router BGP to allow VPN IPv4 routes to be advertised over IPv6 transport with an IPv6 address as the BGP next hop?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia router to advertise VPN IPv4 routes over IPv6 transport with an IPv6 address as the BGP next hop, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        family vpn-ipv4
        advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4
        extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
        next-hop-self
exit
```

Additionally, if you need to ensure proper next-hop resolution for these routes:
```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes
    allow-static
    transport-tunnel family vpn
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. This configuration enables the required capabilities for VPN IPv4 route advertisement with IPv6 next hops over IPv6 transport.
