To configure a Nokia router to advertise a long-lived stale time of 86400 seconds in BGP graceful restart LLGR capability, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    long-lived
        advertised-stale-time 86400
exit all
```

If you also want to enable LLGR stale route advertisement to all neighbors (including those without LLGR capability), add:
```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    long-lived
        advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors
exit all
```
