To configure BGP on your Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes received from EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

If you need to enable sending these aggregated values back to EBGP peers, also include:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. These commands will enable the router to accept, aggregate, and optionally send link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes with EBGP peers.
