How to enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes spanning multiple ASes on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes spanning multiple ASes on a Nokia router, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        aigp
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your specific BGP group name. This enables the Accumulated IGP (AIGP) path attribute for BGP peers in the specified group, allowing path selection to consider end-to-end IGP metrics across multiple ASes.

For additional optimization, you may also want to configure:

```
configure router bgp
    multipath 8
    ibgp-multipath
    best-path-selection
        ebgp-ibgp-equal
    exit
exit
```

These commands enable multipath support, IBGP multipath load balancing, and equal consideration of EBGP/IBGP paths in best path selection.
