To enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics in Nokia routers, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-router-id
    exit
exit
```

This configuration ensures that BGP path selection will prioritize routes based on IGP metrics rather than comparing router IDs when selecting paths. The `ignore-router-id` command makes BGP skip the router-ID comparison step in the best-path selection algorithm, allowing other attributes like IGP cost to take precedence.
