To tie the BGP session state with the underlying BFD session at the neighbor level on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            bfd-enable
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This configuration enables BFD for the specific BGP neighbor, linking the BGP session state to the BFD session state.
