To enable BGP routing protocol on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
exit
```

This will create the BGP protocol instance and enable it administratively. 

If you need to configure additional BGP parameters such as groups, neighbors, or prefix limits, you would continue within the `bgp` context. For example:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <ip-address>
                family ipv4
                prefix-limit ipv4 100000 threshold 75 idle-timeout 30
                no passive
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```
