Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure a Nokia router's BGP group with route reflector cluster ID 192.168.10.5 and ORR location 8 allowing local fallback:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        cluster 192.168.10.5 orr-location 8 allow-local-fallback
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. This configuration will:
1. Set the route reflector cluster ID to 192.168.10.5
2. Configure ORR location 8 for this cluster
3. Enable local fallback behavior when no optimal routes are available from the specified ORR location
