To configure your Nokia router to prefer BGP routes with a Valid origin validation state over NotFound or Invalid states during best path selection, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        compare-origin-validation-state
        origin-invalid-unusable
    exit
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Enable comparison of origin validation states during BGP best path selection
2. Mark routes with Invalid origin validation states as unusable

The router will now prioritize routes in this order: Valid > NotFound > Invalid (with Invalid routes being excluded from consideration).
