To suppress unstable route advertisements in BGP while maintaining convergence of stable routes, use the `min-route-advertisement` command to set a minimum interval between route updates. The recommended value is typically 30 seconds (default), but you can adjust it based on your needs.  

Here’s the CLI configuration:  

```
configure router bgp
    min-route-advertisement 30
exit
```

For more granular control, apply this setting at the group or neighbor level:  

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    min-route-advertisement 30
exit
```

Or:  

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    min-route-advertisement 30
exit
```

This ensures unstable routes are not advertised too frequently, while stable routes continue to converge normally.
------------
