To originate a default BGP route (0.0.0.0/0) towards specific peers in a Nokia router's BGP configuration, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            default-route-target
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of the specific peer you want to send the default route to. This configuration will advertise the default route only to the specified peers.
