To originate a default BGP route towards specific peers on Nokia routers, use the following CLI configuration commands:

1. Enter the BGP configuration context:
```bash
configure router bgp
```

2. Create or select a BGP group (if it doesn't exist):
```bash
group <group-name>
```

3. Add the specific neighbor(s) to which you want to send the default route:
```bash
neighbor <peer-ip-address>
```

4. Enable the default route origination for the neighbor(s):
```bash
default-route-target
```

5. Exit the configuration contexts:
```bash
exit all
```

Example for sending a default route to peer 192.0.2.1 in group "PEER-GROUP":
```bash
configure router bgp
group "PEER-GROUP"
neighbor 192.0.2.1
default-route-target
exit all
```
