To prevent BGP peers from using 4-byte autonomous system numbers on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration command:

```
configure router bgp disable-4byte-asn
```

This command can be applied at three levels:
1. Global BGP level (`config>router>bgp`)
2. BGP group level (`config>router>bgp>group`)
3. Individual neighbor level (`config>router>bgp>group>neighbor`)

For example, to apply it to a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group GROUP_NAME disable-4byte-asn
```

Or to a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group GROUP_NAME neighbor IP_ADDRESS disable-4byte-asn
```
------------
