## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to strictly support only IPv4 routing exchanges with a BGP peer by preventing new capability negotiations?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to strictly support only IPv4 routing exchanges with a BGP peer by preventing new capability negotiations, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            disable-capability-negotiation
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of your BGP peer. This configuration will ensure only IPv4 routing exchanges are supported and disable any new capability negotiations with the specified peer.
