To prevent BGP from immediately dropping sessions when an external link failure is detected, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    disable-fast-external-failover
exit
```

This command disables the fast external failover behavior, allowing BGP to wait for the hold timer to expire before declaring the session down, rather than reacting immediately to link failures. 

The command can also be applied at the group or neighbor level if needed:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    disable-fast-external-failover
exit
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    disable-fast-external-failover
exit
```
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to prevent BGP from immediately dropping sessions when an external link failure is detected?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent BGP from immediately dropping sessions when an external link failure is detected, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    disable-fast-external-failover
exit
```

This command disables the fast external failover behavior, allowing BGP to wait for the hold timer to expire before declaring the session down, rather than reacting immediately to link failures. 

The command can also be applied at the group or neighbor level if needed:

