To prevent immediate BGP session teardown upon link failure detection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    disable-fast-external-failover
exit
```

This command disables the fast external failover feature, allowing the BGP session to remain stable during transient link failures instead of immediately tearing down the session.
