To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix <ip-prefix/prefix-length>
        exit
        dynamic-neighbor-limit <peers>
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP peer group name, `<ip-prefix/prefix-length>` with the network range from which to accept dynamic peers, and `<peers>` with the maximum number of dynamic sessions allowed (1-8192).

Optionally, you may want to add:
```bash
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        initial-send-delay-zero
        prefix-limit ipv4 <limit> threshold <percentage> idle-timeout <minutes>
exit
```

This additional configuration sets immediate UPDATE sending after session establishment and configures prefix limits for IPv4 routes. Adjust the values (`<limit>`, `<percentage>`, `<minutes>`) according to your requirements.
