To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix <ip-prefix/prefix-length>
        exit
        dynamic-neighbor-limit <peers>
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP peer group name, `<ip-prefix/prefix-length>` with the network prefix from which to accept dynamic neighbors, and `<peers>` with the maximum number of dynamic sessions allowed for this group (1-8192).

Optionally, you can add:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        initial-send-delay-zero
exit
```
to enable immediate UPDATE message sending after session establishment.

For prefix limits on dynamic neighbors:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        prefix-limit <family> <limit> [threshold <percentage>] [idle-timeout <minutes>|forever|log-only]
exit
```
