To configure BGP origin validation for both labeled IPv6 routes and unlabeled IPv4 routes from a peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip>
            enable-origin-validation ipv4 label-ipv6
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip>` with the IP address of the peer. This will enable origin validation for:
- Unlabeled IPv4 routes (via `ipv4` parameter)
- Labeled IPv6 routes (via `label-ipv6` parameter)
