To configure a Nokia router to immediately drop a BGP peer when its resolving route is removed from the IP routing table, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp enable-peer-tracking
```

This command enables BGP peer tracking, which ensures the BGP peer is dropped immediately if the route used to resolve its address is removed, without waiting for the hold timer to expire.  

Apply this under the global BGP context, group, or neighbor level depending on your specific requirements. For example, to apply it to a specific neighbor:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> enable-peer-tracking
```
------------
