To configure a Nokia router to verify that the last ASN in the AS_PATH of all EBGP routes matches the peer's configured AS and handle mismatches appropriately, use the following CLI commands:

1. Configure the peer's AS number:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> peer-as <as-number>
```

2. Enable enforcement of the first AS in the AS_PATH:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> enforce-first-as
```
or at the neighbor level:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> enforce-first-as
```

3. Set the desired behavior for handling mismatches:
   - To reset the session when a mismatch occurs (default behavior):
     ```
     configure router bgp update-fault-tolerance disable
     ```
   - To keep the session up but treat mismatched routes as withdrawn:
     ```
     configure router bgp update-fault-tolerance enable
     ```

These commands will ensure that all EBGP routes are validated against the peer's configured AS number, with the specified action taken for any mismatches.
