To enable the updated BGP error handling procedures on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    error-handling
        update-fault-tolerance
    exit
exit
```

This will apply the non-disruptive error handling approaches for BGP UPDATE messages at the global BGP level. If needed, you can also configure this at the group or neighbor level by navigating to `config>router>bgp>group` or `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor` respectively before entering the `error-handling` context.
