To configure your Nokia router to apply the "INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY" for controlling outbound BGP routes, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        export "INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY"
```

If you need to apply this policy to a specific BGP group or neighbor, use these variations:

For a BGP group:
```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            export "INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY"
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <ip-address>
                export "INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY"
```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<ip-address>` with your actual BGP group name and neighbor IP address respectively.
