To enable extended community-based BGP filtering in outbound route filtering on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

1. At the global BGP level:
```bash
configure router bgp outbound-route-filtering
    extended-community
exit
```

2. For a specific BGP group:
```bash
configure router bgp group <group-name> outbound-route-filtering
    extended-community
exit
```

3. For a specific BGP neighbor:
```bash
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> outbound-route-filtering
    extended-community
exit
```

These commands will enable extended community-based filtering for outbound BGP routes at the respective levels. The configuration can be applied globally, per group, or per neighbor depending on your requirements.
