To configure extended community-based BGP filtering in outbound route filtering on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

1. Enable outbound route filtering at the desired level (BGP instance, group, or neighbor):
```cli
configure router bgp outbound-route-filtering
```

2. Enable extended community support within outbound route filtering:
```cli
extended-community
```

For example, if you want to configure this for a specific BGP group and its neighbor:
```cli
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME" outbound-route-filtering
extended-community
exit
neighbor "NEIGHBOR_IP" outbound-route-filtering
extended-community
exit exit exit
```

Remember that by default, extended community support is disabled in outbound route filtering, so these commands explicitly enable it.
