To configure a Nokia router to report both IPv6 unicast (labeled) and IPv4 VPN (SAFI 128) address families to a BMP monitoring station, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure
    bmp
        station "BMP_STATION_NAME"
            family label-ipv6 vpn-ipv4
            connection
                local-address <local_ip_address>
                remote-address <monitoring_station_ip>
                no shutdown
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace:
- `BMP_STATION_NAME` with your preferred name for the BMP station
- `<local_ip_address>` with the router's local IP address to be used for BMP communication
- `<monitoring_station_ip>` with the IP address of your BMP monitoring station

This configuration enables reporting of both the IPv6 labeled unicast (label-ipv6) and IPv4 VPN (vpn-ipv4) address families to the specified BMP monitoring station.
