To enable BGP graceful restart helper functionality for IPv6 routes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
exit
```

If you want to customize the behavior further, you can optionally configure additional parameters such as stale route timeout or enable notification support:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 300
        enable-notification
    exit
exit
```

These commands will enable BGP graceful restart helper functionality globally for all supported address families, including IPv6, as long as both peers advertise the GR capability.
