To create a BGP peer group named "EU-West-1" on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group "EU-West-1"
exit
```

This will create the BGP peer group "EU-West-1". You can then further configure the group by specifying its type (internal/external), adding neighbors, or setting other parameters as needed. For example, to set the group as internal:

```
configure router bgp
    group "EU-West-1"
        type internal
    exit
exit
```
