To configure a Nokia router to enforce a locally-defined restart time of 300 seconds for all AFI/SAFI included in the peer's GR capability during long-lived graceful restart, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart long-lived
    helper-override-restart-time 300
exit
```

This will override the peer's advertised restart time with your locally configured value of 300 seconds for all AFI/SAFI included in the peer's GR capability.
