To configure a Nokia router to impose a local LLGR stale time of 3600 seconds while overriding the peer-advertised value, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart long-lived
    helper-override-stale-time 3600
exit
```

This configuration will apply the local LLGR stale time of 3600 seconds globally across all address families. If you need to specify different values per address family, you would enter the family context under `long-lived` and configure the override there. For example:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart long-lived family ipv4
    helper-override-stale-time 3600
exit
```
