## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to prevent BGP from considering the resolved distance to the next-hop when comparing routes with the same NLRI from base router BGP peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent BGP from considering the resolved distance to the next-hop when comparing routes with the same NLRI from base router BGP peers, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    ignore-nh-metric
exit
``` 

This command disables the consideration of the IGP metric to the BGP next-hop in the BGP best path selection process for routes learned from base router BGP peers.
