To configure BGP on a Nokia router to announce reachability information immediately after session establishment with peers, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp initial-send-delay-zero
```

This command ensures that UPDATE messages are sent to peers as soon as the BGP sessions are established. You can apply it globally under `config>router>bgp`, at the group level under `config>router>bgp>group`, or for specific neighbors under `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor`.
------------
