To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 paths per unlabeled IPv6 unicast prefix and negotiate to receive multiple routes per prefix, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables the BGP add-paths capability for unlabeled IPv6 unicast routes, sets the maximum advertised paths to 8 per prefix, and negotiates to receive multiple routes per prefix.
