To enter the context for configuring labeled route options in BGP next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution
    labeled-routes
        transport-tunnel
            family label-ipv4
```

This sequence will take you to the correct context for configuring next-hop resolution options for labeled-unicast IPv4 routes. If you need to configure IPv6 instead, replace `label-ipv4` with `label-ipv6`. For VPN routes, use `vpn` as the family parameter.
