To configure the Nokia router to use the IP address 192.0.2.1 as the source for BGP communication within a group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
local-address 192.0.2.1
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the actual name of your BGP group. This sets 192.0.2.1 as the local address for all BGP communications within the specified group.
