Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable BGP Long-Lived Graceful-Restart (LLGR) functionality on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
        stale-routes-time <time>
        restart-time <seconds>
        enable-notification
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<time>` with the desired duration in seconds (1-3600) for maintaining stale routes, and `<seconds>` with the restart-time value (0-4095) to advertise in the graceful-restart capability. 

For example:
```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
        stale-routes-time 1800
        restart-time 600
        enable-notification
    exit
exit
```
