To configure a Nokia router to silently discard BGP routes containing its own AS number in the AS path without terminating the peering session, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> loop-detect discard-route
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This will apply the setting to a specific neighbor. Alternatively, you can apply it at the group level:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> loop-detect discard-route
```

Or globally for all BGP peers:

```
configure router bgp loop-detect discard-route
```
