To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes with MED values derived from IGP cost, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    med-out igp-cost
exit
```

This will set the MED value to match the IGP cost for all BGP routes advertised to peers. The configuration can be applied at the global BGP level, group level, or neighbor level depending on your specific requirements.
