To disable the monitoring of BGP sessions on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

1. To disable BGP monitoring globally:
```
configure router bgp
no monitor
exit
```

2. Alternatively, if you want to disable monitoring for a specific BGP group or neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
no monitor
exit
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
no monitor
exit
```

These commands will stop the monitoring of BGP sessions at the specified level (global, group, or neighbor).
------------
