To configure the TTL value to 128 for EBGP packets when the peer is multiple hops away on a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <peer-ip> multihop 128
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip>` with the IP address of the EBGP peer. This sets the TTL value in outgoing packets to 128 for the specified EBGP neighbor.
