## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia router to advertise up to 3 different paths per multicast VPN IPv6 prefix and negotiate to receive multiple paths, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        mvpn-ipv6 send 3 receive
    exit
exit
```

If you need to apply this configuration at the group or neighbor level instead of globally, replace `config>router>bgp>add-paths` with either:
- `config>router>bgp>group>add-paths` for a specific BGP group, or  
- `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>add-paths` for a specific BGP neighbor

The command structure remains the same (`mvpn-ipv6 send 3 receive`) within those contexts.
