Here are the CLI commands to configure a BGP peer with IP address 192.0.2.1 on a Nokia router:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor 192.0.2.1
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP group name. 

To further customize the peer configuration, you can add parameters like:
```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            type external
            neighbor 192.0.2.1
                prefix-limit ipv4 500000 threshold 75 idle-timeout 30
```

This example configures the peer as external and sets a prefix limit of 500,000 IPv4 routes with a 75% threshold and 30-minute idle timeout. Adjust these values according to your requirements.
