To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes to a specific neighbor using the local BGP instance address as the next-hop, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip-address>
            next-hop-self
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip-address>` with the specific neighbor's IP address. The `next-hop-self` command ensures that the local BGP instance address is used as the next-hop for advertised routes to this neighbor.
