To configure your Nokia router to preserve BGP next-hop information for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes when advertising to peers in a specific group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
        advertise-ipv6-next-hops label-ipv4 label-ipv6
        next-hop-unchanged label-ipv4 label-ipv6
exit all
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP peer group. This configuration:
1. Enables extended next-hop encoding for labeled IPv4 routes
2. Allows IPv6 next-hops to be advertised for both labeled IPv4 and IPv6 routes
3. Preserves the original next-hop information for both labeled IPv4 and IPv6 routes when advertising to peers in this group
