## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP prefix-based filtering capability for exchanging routes with peers on Nokia routers, use the following CLI configuration commands:

1. Enable outbound route filtering at the BGP level:
```
configure router bgp outbound-route-filtering
```

2. Apply prefix limits to control the number of routes accepted from a peer (example for IPv4):
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> prefix-limit ipv4 <max-routes> threshold <percentage>
```

3. Configure import policies to filter incoming routes (replace `<policy-name>` with your actual policy):
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> import "<policy-name>"
```

These commands will enable prefix-based filtering capabilities for BGP peering sessions. You can apply them at the global BGP level, group level, or specific neighbor level depending on your requirements.
