To disable BGP session initiation attempts for a specific neighbor, use the `passive` command under the neighbor configuration:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> passive
```

This will prevent the router from initiating BGP connections to the specified neighbor while still allowing it to accept incoming connections if initiated by the neighbor.
