To configure the Nokia router to tear down BGP sessions when the route to a neighbor address is not accepted by the policy named "core-routes", use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-address>
            family ipv4
                prefix-limit ipv4 1 post-import
                    idle-timeout forever
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Then apply the import policy "core-routes" to the neighbor:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-address>
            import "core-routes"
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration will:
1. Set a prefix limit of 1 for IPv4 routes with `post-import` flag
2. Configure the session to stay down forever if the limit is hit
3. Apply your "core-routes" import policy to control which routes are accepted

When the route to the neighbor is not accepted by the "core-routes" policy, the BGP session will be torn down and won't automatically reconnect.
