To configure your Nokia router to send a warning message when receiving 5000 IPv6 routes from a peer at an 80% threshold without terminating the BGP session, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family ipv6
                prefix-limit 5000 threshold 80 log-only
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of your BGP peer. This configuration will:
1. Set a limit of 5000 IPv6 routes
2. Trigger a warning message at 4000 routes (80% of 5000)
3. Continue operating normally even if the limit is reached (`log-only` parameter prevents session termination)
