Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure your Nokia router for the requested BGP IPv6 prefix limits:

```
configure router bgp
    group <your-group-name>
        neighbor <peer-IP-address>
            family ipv6
                prefix-limit ipv6 5000 threshold 75 log-only
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration will:
- Allow a maximum of 5000 IPv6 routes from the BGP peer
- Set a warning threshold at 3750 routes (75% of 5000)
- Keep the BGP session active even if the limit is reached
- Generate log events when both the 75% threshold and the 5000 route limit are reached
