To configure your Nokia router to accept dynamic BGP sessions from peers within the 192.168.100.0/24 subnet, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group DYNAMIC_PEERS
            dynamic-neighbor
                prefix 192.168.100.0/24
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

If you want to set a limit on the number of dynamic BGP sessions from this subnet (for example, limiting to 50 peers), add:
```
configure router
    bgp
        group DYNAMIC_PEERS
            dynamic-neighbor-limit 50
        exit
    exit
```

For immediate BGP updates to new peers, enable:
```
configure router
    bgp
        group DYNAMIC_PEERS
            initial-send-delay-zero
        exit
    exit
```
