To configure the primary IPv4 address as 192.168.10.1 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp optimal-route-reflection
location 1 primary-ip-address 192.168.10.1
exit all
```

Replace `1` with your desired location ID (values 1-16) if needed. This will set 192.168.10.1 as the primary IPv4 address for the specified location in the BGP optimal route reflection configuration.
