To configure a Nokia router to remove private ASNs in BGP updates while preserving private ASN 64512 when it matches the peer's AS number, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            peer-as 64512
            remove-private skip-peer-as
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This configuration will remove private ASNs from the AS path while keeping ASN 64512 if it matches the peer's AS number.
