To configure your Nokia router to bind BGP label routes only to the subset of tunnel types specified under `resolution-filter`, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family
    resolution filter
    resolution-filter [tunnel-types]
exit all
```

Replace `[tunnel-types]` with the specific tunnel types you want to allow (e.g., `bgp`, `ldp`, `rsvp`, `sr-isis`, `sr-ospf`, `sr-policy`, or `sr-te`). For example, if you only want to allow BGP and RSVP tunnels:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family
    resolution filter
    resolution-filter bgp rsvp
exit all
```
