To configure a Nokia router to enable resolution of unlabeled IPv4 BGP routes using tunnel types under BGP next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter bgp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
            use-bgp-routes
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable BGP route usage for recursive next-hop resolution (`use-bgp-routes`)
2. Configure IPv4 family under shortcut-tunnel for unlabeled IPv4 routes
3. Specify BGP as the tunnel type for resolution (`resolution-filter bgp`)

You can add other tunnel types (like ldp, rsvp, etc.) to the `resolution-filter` if needed.
