To administratively disable a BGP neighbor on a Nokia router without removing its configuration, use the `passive` command under the neighbor context. Here's the CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> passive
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This will prevent the router from initiating connections to the specified neighbor while maintaining all configuration settings.
