To administratively disable a BGP neighbor on a Nokia router without removing its configuration, use the `shutdown` command under the specific neighbor configuration. Here's the CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> shutdown
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This will disable the BGP session while preserving all other configuration settings for that neighbor.

To re-enable the neighbor later, use:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> no shutdown
```
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
"How to administratively disable a BGP neighbor on a Nokia router without removing its configuration?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To administratively disable a BGP neighbor on a Nokia router without removing its configuration, use the `shutdown` command under the specific neighbor configuration. Here's the CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> shutdown
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This will disable the BGP session while preserving all other configuration settings for that neighbor.

To re-enable the neighbor later, use:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> no shutdown
---
