To prevent BGP routes from being reflected back to the sending peer on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration command under the specific BGP group or neighbor:

```bash
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> disable-client-reflect
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the IP address of the neighbor you want to configure. This command ensures that the route reflector does not send routes back to the originating client.
------------
