To prevent BGP routes from being reflected back to the originating peer on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

1. If the peer is a route reflector client:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> disable-client-reflect
```

2. Alternatively, to handle route loops more generally:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> loop-detect discard-route
```

These commands will either disable route reflection specifically for that client or discard any looped routes from the peer.
------------
