To configure your Nokia router to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference OSPF instance for BGP next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunn family ipv4
                resolution-filter sr-ospf
            exit
            labeled-routes transport-tunnel family ipv4
                resolution-filter sr-ospf
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

For IPv6, replace `sr-ospf` with `sr-ospf3` in both resolution filters if needed. This configuration ensures BGP will prioritize SR tunnels from the lowest preference OSPF instance (or lowest-numbered instance in case of a tie) for next-hop resolution.
