To enable BGP on a Nokia router to advertise locally configured non-local segment routing policies as originated routes to BGP peers supporting the SR policy IPv4 address family, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    sr-policy-import
    graceful-restart
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
    group <group-name>
        family sr-policy-ipv4
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family sr-policy-ipv4
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of your BGP peer. This configuration enables the import of static SR policies into BGP, advertises them to peers supporting the SR Policy IPv4 address family, and ensures proper next-hop encoding capabilities.
