To configure Nokia routers to maintain stale BGP routes for 300 seconds during graceful restart, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    stale-routes-time 300
exit
```

This will set the stale routes retention time to 300 seconds globally for all BGP peers under graceful restart. 

If you need to apply this setting to a specific BGP group or neighbor instead, use these variations:

For a BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> graceful-restart
    stale-routes-time 300
exit
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> graceful-restart
    stale-routes-time 300
exit
```
