To configure TCP keepalive parameters for the station on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure
bmp
station
connection
tcp-keepalive
keep-idle 600
keep-interval 15
keep-count 4
exit all
```

These commands will set:
- The initial idle time before sending the first keepalive probe to 600 seconds
- The interval between subsequent keepalive probes to 15 seconds
- The number of missed keepalives before declaring the connection down to 4

The values shown are the defaults; adjust them according to your specific requirements.
