To configure a Nokia router to preserve the original BGP next-hop when advertising routes between EBGP peers within the same IP subnet, use the following CLI commands:

1. Enable `third-party-nexthop` at the BGP level or per neighbor:
   ```cli
   configure router bgp third-party-nexthop
   ```
   Or for a specific neighbor:
   ```cli
   configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> third-party-nexthop
   ```

2. Ensure `next-hop-self` is disabled (default behavior):
   ```cli
   configure router bgp group <group-name> no next-hop-self
   ```

3. Optionally, disable `next-hop-unchanged` if it was previously enabled (default is disabled):
   ```cli
   configure router bgp group <group-name> no next-hop-unchanged
   ```

These settings will ensure the original BGP next-hop is preserved for EBGP peers in the same subnet.
