To configure your Nokia router to preserve the original BGP next-hop when advertising routes between EBGP peers within the same subnet, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp
    third-party-nexthop
exit
```

Alternatively, if you want to apply this setting to a specific BGP group or neighbor, use:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    third-party-nexthop
exit
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    third-party-nexthop
exit
```

These commands will ensure the BGP next-hop remains unchanged when advertising routes between EBGP peers in the same subnet.
