To configure your Nokia router to only accept incoming BGP packets with a TTL value of at least 64, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    ttl-security 64
```

or for a specific neighbor:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    ttl-security 64
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address if applying to a specific neighbor.
