To configure a BGP peer as external on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

1. Enter the BGP configuration context:
```
configure router bgp
```

2. Create a BGP group (if it doesn't exist) and set its type to external:
```
group <group-name> type external
```

3. Add the specific neighbor to the group:
```
neighbor <peer-ip-address>
```

For example, to create an external BGP peer group named "EBGP-PEERS" with neighbor 192.0.2.1:
```
configure router bgp
group EBGP-PEERS type external
neighbor 192.0.2.1
exit all
```
