To configure a BGP peer as an external neighbor on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type external
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the actual IP address of your external BGP peer.

If you need to enable additional features like disabling fast external failover or neighbor trust for VPN families, you can add these commands:

```
configure router bgp
    disable-fast-external-failover
    neighbor-trust vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
    group <group-name>
        type external
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
    exit
exit
```
