To configure Nokia routers to handle BGP UPDATE message errors non-disruptively when no length errors prevent NLRI field parsing, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp error-handling
    update-fault-tolerance
exit
```

This enables the `treat-as-withdraw` behavior for UPDATE message errors while ensuring NLRI fields can still be parsed correctly. The configuration can also be applied at the group or neighbor level if needed:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> error-handling
    update-fault-tolerance
exit

configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> error-handling
    update-fault-tolerance
exit
```
