To enable recursive resolution of BGP next-hops for unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 routes using BGP routes, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            use-bgp-routes
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration will allow the router to use BGP routes for resolving the next-hop of unlabeled IPv4 and IPv6 routes, supporting up to four levels of recursion. The default behavior is disabled (`no use-bgp-routes`), so this command explicitly enables the feature.
